1
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,897
YAMOO! YAMOO! YAMOO! YAMOO!

2
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:29,880
YAMOO!

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,420
It's time to duel!

5
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:13,327
Man, this dualist kingdom looks
like a pretty big place, Yugi.

6
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:16,367
Finding your grandpa is
not going to be easy.

7
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,619
Well, we've got to start somewhere.

8
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,340
Whoa, check out the suits.

9
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:36,886
Attention all duelists, please
disembark in an orderly fashion.

10
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:41,157
Hey, Taya, what if one of those security
guys finds out we're both stowaways?

11
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:43,437
We oughta just play it safe and swim back.

12
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,597
We're in the middle of
nowhere, lame brain.

13
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,621
If you can just try and
act normal, we'll be okay.

14
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:53,980
Just act cool, act cool.

15
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:56,520
Cool as a cucumber, keep it cool.

16
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:58,090
Hey, you!

17
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,017
Don't look so nervous.

18
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,477
You guys are our guests here.

19
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:04,390
That's right.

20
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:05,720
I'm your guest.

21
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,400
I think I just had a heart attack.

22
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,977
Way to play it cool, Tristan.

23
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:16,825
That wasn't suspicious at all.

24
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,137
All right.

25
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,137
Every single one of us made it here.

26
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:21,320
Safe and...

27
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:27,067
You would never have caught that
cold if it wasn't for Weevil.

28
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,477
Say goodbye to Exodium!

29
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,390
My cards!

30
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,820
Those were the Exodia cards
that my grandpa gave me.

31
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:34,810
I'll get them.

32
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:36,050
Joey, don't!

33
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:39,117
Speaking of our wormy friend,

34
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,837
looks like he just
slithered his way off the

35
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,117
boat and is already looking
to start some trouble.

36
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,317
That slimeball, I'd love to
wipe that smirk off his face.

37
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,812
I would, too, but we don't
have time for Weevil right now.

38
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,160
Welcome, all duelists, please.

39
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,920
Follow the stairs to meet your host.

40
00:02:58,340 --> 00:03:00,800
That castle's gotta belong to Pegasus.

41
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,666
Then what are we waiting for?

42
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,020
Huh? What's that?

43
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:14,590
Huh?

44
00:03:14,673 --> 00:03:15,503
What do you see, Taya?

45
00:03:15,586 --> 00:03:16,940
It looked like Bakura.

46
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,860
Bakura? From school?

47
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,366
Again with this Bakura stuff?

48
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:22,619
Where is he, Taya?

49
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:27,420
That's two times that I've seen him
now, But he's not there anymore.

50
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,049
Maybe it's all in my head.

51
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:32,107
Come on, we're on a
rescue mission, remember?

52
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,600
Wow, look, that's Weevil Underwood.

53
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:43,328
He's the regional champion.

54
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:46,760
And that's the runner-up Rex Raptor.

55
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,780
And there's Mikko Tsunami.

56
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,096
He was ranked third.

57
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,957
Wow, these are all the
best duelists in the world.

58
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,517
But where's the world champion, Kaiba?

59
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,541
Didn't you hear?

60
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:56,637
Some kid beat him.

61
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,797
On his own turf, too.

62
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:58,710
Are you serious?

63
00:03:58,793 --> 00:04:00,037
I thought Kaiba was the best.

64
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,580
He was, but not anymore.

65
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,371
Yugi's supposed to be the kid to beat now.

66
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:05,690
Attention.

67
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,035
Please gather around.

68
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:10,282
Your benevolent host is
anxious to greet you all.

69
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:21,486
Boy, would I like to get just
five minutes alone with that guy.

70
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:33,040
When next we duel, we shall
play for far higher stakes.

71
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,597
You see, I have found that
given the proper incentive,

72
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:39,220
anyone can be made to play my game.

73
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:47,210
Yogi!

74
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:48,850
Grandpa!

75
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:54,479
I'm not leaving this island
until I save my grandpa.

76
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:57,071
no matter what Pegasus has planned for me.

77
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,340
Greetings, duelists.

78
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:09,700
I am Maximilian Pegasus.

79
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:14,580
It is my great honor and pleasure to
welcome you all to the duelist kingdom.

80
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:18,240
You stand before me, the
world's greatest duelists.

81
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:22,657
But come tournament's end, only
one shall be crowned king of games.

82
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:26,580
I implore you all to assemble
your dueling decks with care,

83
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:30,100
with creativity, and with cunning.

84
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:33,988
For this competition will test
your skills like never before.

85
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:38,617
To track your progress in the tournament,
you've each been given a dueling glove.

86
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:41,457
You've also been given
two precious star chips.

87
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:44,817
You must wager these star chips
on each duel you compete in.

88
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:49,557
To advance to the final level of competition
for a chance at the $3 million prize,

89
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,660
you must win 10 star chips.

90
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:55,117
Ten star chips will
admit you into my castle,

91
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,494
where you'll face me in one final duel.

92
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:01,397
If Grandpa's here, I'd bet my dueling
club he's hidden away in that castle.

93
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:04,837
But I'll never be able to get in
there with all the guards around.

94
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:08,685
We're just going to have to win
enough star chips to get inside.

95
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:13,417
This will be a tournament unlike
anything you have ever experienced.

96
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:16,853
State-of-the-art dueling arenas
cover this entire island.

97
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,517
And intriguing new dueling
rules will be in effect.

98
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,717
I could tell you what these new rules are.

99
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,640
But what fun would that be?

100
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:27,704
You'll discover them as you compete,
or you won't last very long.

101
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:32,640
Remember, play boldly, think
strategically, and duel mercilessly.

102
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:36,782
You have one full hour to prepare,
both your cards and yourselves.

103
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:40,900
When the skies light up with
fireworks, the duels will begin.

104
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:45,420
The duelists have arrived,

105
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:49,360
Yugi has taken the bait, and
the games are about to begin.

106
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,420
Everything goes according to plan.

107
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,580
I gotta win my way into that castle.

108
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,140
I just gotta.

109
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,597
Yugi, I don't know if
I can win this thing.

110
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:05,337
Maybe it'd be best for you
to take your start ship back.

111
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:06,420
Nah, you keep it.

112
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:10,277
Your little sister's counting on you to
win the tournament's prize money for her.

113
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,190
Thanks, man.

114
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,580
You can do it.

115
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:15,697
You just gotta steer clear of the
more experienced duelists at first.

116
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:17,937
Yeah, it's just a matter
of working your way up.

117
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,260
Thanks, you guys.

118
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:24,757
Well, Yugi, between your grandpa and my
sister, we don't have any room for mistakes.

119
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,670
Right.

120
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,780
The fireworks! It's starting!

121
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:32,780
Let's do it!

122
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,520
So, what's your plan, Yugi?

123
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:40,997
Well, I might as well stick with Weevil.

124
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:43,337
After all, we do have a score to settle.

125
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:45,067
I was hoping you'd say that.

126
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,440
Isn't that him? Huh?

127
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,710
Weevil!

128
00:07:48,793 --> 00:07:51,620
Weevil, I challenge you
to a duel! Hey, wait!

129
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:55,031
I can't believe it, Weevil's running away!

130
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,760
Hey, wait up!

131
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:04,757
Where are all these moths coming from?

132
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,252
Ugh, they're disgusting!

133
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:08,700
He's fast for a small guy!

134
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:11,200
Maybe you're just slow for a big guy!

135
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,977
We're never gonna catch him.

136
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,937
As long as the whole island's in
bounds, he'll keep running all day!

137
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,457
Hey, what's Weevil up to?

138
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:20,317
He's wanted to duel with me
ever since we met on the boat.

139
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,871
So what's he running for?

140
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:23,970
Wait a minute.

141
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:26,667
What did he say on the boat?

142
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,717
Everyone will soon
learn that there are new

143
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:31,565
rules on the island that
require more strategy.

144
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:34,517
It must have something
to do with the new rules.

145
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,247
So I better figure out what.

146
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:37,520
And fast.

147
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:42,380
There he is. Welcome.

148
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,237
Sent the spider to the fly.

149
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:47,460
You flew right into my trap. Again!

150
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:51,832
It's time you answer for what
you did on the boat, Weevil.

151
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:10,180
All right, Weevil.

152
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:13,217
Time to find out if you're as good at
dueling as you are at running away.

153
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:17,280
Was I simply running away or
cleverly weaving you into my web?

154
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,860
It's time to duel.

155
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:22,200
As you wish!

156
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,660
Ah, it's an earthquake!

157
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,360
What have you done?

158
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:41,100
Whoa!

159
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,600
The entire ground is transforming!

160
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:53,100
It's gigantic!

161
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:00,495
Man, these aren't going to
be like the duels back home.

162
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:06,640
You've just stepped into a hornet's
nest, and there's no way out!

163
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:07,900
What is that?

164
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:11,197
These giant arenas must be
set up all over the island.

165
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:13,162
I'll just meet you on the field.

166
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:16,260
I don't like this.

167
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,360
Weevil's a little too cocky.

168
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,980
I noticed that you have
just one starship, Yuki.

169
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:26,997
I guess that means I'll have the pleasure
of eliminating you from the tournament.

170
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:30,457
Once you're gone, everyone else's
chips will be easy pickings.

171
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:33,180
Not if I take your two first. What?

172
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:36,754
This will be an all-or-nothing
match for the both of us.

173
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:38,050
Ha!

174
00:10:38,133 --> 00:10:41,340
Why should I risk both my star
chips when you only have one?

175
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:43,937
Because I have something
else I think you want.

176
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:46,120
My whole Duel Monsters deck.

177
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:48,740
So, you'd risk your grandpa's deck?

178
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:49,860
Fine with me.

179
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:55,677
Winning all your cards will be an easy
way to exterminate you once and for all.

180
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:56,590
Exterminate?

181
00:10:56,673 --> 00:10:58,574
Swat that little twerp like a mosquito.

182
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:02,157
Whoa, sounds like a duel is
about to start over there.

183
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,680
That's Weevil Underwood.

184
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:05,272
But who's the other guy?

185
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,520
That guy is Yugi Moto.

186
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:08,800
He beat Kaiba.

187
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,420
And I happen to be his
best friend, Joey Wheeler.

188
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:15,093
And these two, these two are trespasses.

189
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:18,637
I thought I wouldn't be seeing a
Weevil-Yugi match up till the finals.

190
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,197
Weevil's the regional champ.

191
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,357
No new kid's got a chance against him.

192
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:26,360
Well, Yu-Gi, my adoring public
is waiting, so we should begin!

193
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,393
Let's see how you like my killer needle.

194
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:44,296
You'll have to get through
my mammoth graveyard first.

195
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:51,060
This massive monster will match your
annoying insect point for point.

196
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,430
Attack!

197
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:57,780
Killer Needle, let's show the
mammoth your stinger. Attack!

198
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,610
No!

199
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:03,750
Ha!

200
00:12:03,833 --> 00:12:04,800
Gone after one sting?

201
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:07,160
He must be allergic. I don't get it.

202
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:09,417
Both creatures were evenly matched.

203
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:10,877
It should have been a stalemate.

204
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:15,760
Have you begun to figure out yet why I
led you all the way to this forest area?

205
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,940
If you just look around,

206
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:23,420
then you will see that this area is an exact
replica of our surrounding environment.

207
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:26,400
One part wasteland and one part forest.

208
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,520
And who thrives in the forest?

209
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:30,010
Bugs!

210
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:33,077
The strongest, most powerful
insects rule the forest.

211
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:37,697
So as long as I play my bugs in the
forest area, I get a field power bonus!

212
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:41,577
I guess you just weren't listening
when Pegasus said that this

213
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:45,417
tournament would have exciting new
surprises in store for us Maybe

214
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:48,197
if you were smart enough to
steal the tournament's secret new

215
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:52,221
rules like I did you'd be getting
a field power bonus instead of me

216
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:56,677
He cheated he let us here cuz
he knew he'd have an unfair

217
00:12:56,760 --> 00:13:00,237
advantage Go ahead call me
a cheater You're all just

218
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:02,957
angry that you didn't swipe
the rules yourselves and

219
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:07,400
because you didn't little Yugi
is about to get stung What?

220
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,229
How could you be laughing?

221
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,150
Because.

222
00:13:10,233 --> 00:13:12,964
Take a look at your
ferocious killer needle now.

223
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,190
What?

224
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:17,560
Oh, no! My monster!

225
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,899
What have you done with my monster?

226
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:22,700
This makes no sense.

227
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:25,857
My creature was supercharged
with a field power bonus.

228
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:30,140
But according to this, Yugi's creature
somehow became just as powerful.

229
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:34,397
Looks like my mammoth got a field
power bonus from the wasteland area,

230
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,774
just like your bugs do from the forest.

231
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:40,797
The field point advantage was
supposed to be mine alone.

232
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:43,537
I kept wondering about something
on the boat ride here, Weevil.

233
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:46,577
Why were we traveling to some
remote island just to duel?

234
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:50,777
But as soon as I saw this holographic
display grid, it all came together.

235
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:54,037
Every monster has a type of
field that it does best on,

236
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,657
kind of like a home field advantage.

237
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:58,617
And what makes this
island so special is that

238
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:01,720
it contains every type
of field imaginable.

239
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,680
So when you deliberately
led us to this spot,

240
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,369
you were clearly hoping to get
some kind of field advantage.

241
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:15,608
You're awfully clever to put it
all together like that, Yugi.

242
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:18,191
But figuring out one rule won't be enough.

243
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:22,144
There are surprises hidden under
every rock, and I know them all.

244
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,317
You can't beat him, Yugi.

245
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,797
Don't let that fleece scare you.

246
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:27,220
He's bluffing. Really?

247
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:30,266
Then let's just see how
you handle this bluff.

248
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:37,209
My Hercules beetle will find a
way to crawl under your skin.

249
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,397
Even though I know about
the field power bonus,

250
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:43,656
it's too late to rebuild my deck now.

251
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:46,648
I guess a combo attack
would be my best bet.

252
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,300
I play Feral Imp.

253
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:58,102
And now I'll add this Horn of the Unicorn
so its magic will raise my attack points.

254
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:05,172
You'll have to do a lot better than that.

255
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:07,720
Hercules Beetle attack!

256
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:12,900
Feral Imp, magic lightning attack!

257
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:20,197
Yugi's attack didn't
even phase that thing.

258
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,177
Something's screwy.

259
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:24,457
My imp's magic lightning attack
should have destroyed your beetle.

260
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:26,157
Is this another trick, Weevil?

261
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,380
No, Yugi.

262
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:30,937
I just thought you knew that
all monsters with a field

263
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:35,000
power bonus were also resistant
to any type of magic attack.

264
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:38,917
And since my Hercules beetle easily
deflected your lightning bolt,

265
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,457
he has more than enough power left
to destroy your puny feral imp.

266
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:45,187
And continue to eat away
at your life points.

267
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:49,857
Even that four-eyed tick's
weakest bugs are going to be

268
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:52,937
tough to beat so long as he's
got that field power bonus.

269
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:55,817
Yeah, but it's not exactly
like it can just be turned off.

270
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:57,665
That weevil's a no-good cheat.

271
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,960
It's your turn. Make your move.

272
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:03,257
Maybe I should use my
next monster to defend.

273
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:06,317
By putting my card in defense
mode, my monster will take a hit.

274
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,257
But my life points will be spared.

275
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:10,360
So, we're defending now, are we?

276
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:11,497
Very clever.

277
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:16,420
Since I can't see your monster's defense
points, I can't be sure I can beat it.

278
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:20,540
But even your strongest monster
can't stand against my basic insect.

279
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:25,952
Not only does he get a field power bonus,

280
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:32,160
but I'm upgrading him with a level 3
laser cannon and a level 2 power boost.

281
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,030
No!

282
00:16:35,113 --> 00:16:38,257
His insect's so powerful now,
my defense won't stand a chance.

283
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:40,928
And after it falls, my
life points are next.

284
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:50,909
Now, Yuki, for all the innocent
little bugs you've squashed,

285
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:55,300
stumped, crushed, or
fumigated, it's payback time!

286
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:06,157
You'll have to do better than that if you

287
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:09,160
hope to survive my bug's
laser-powered arsenal.

288
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:10,971
Then I'll play this card.

289
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:17,340
Hmm, another defense card, no doubt.

290
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:20,560
And I'll make sure that
defending is all he can do.

291
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:23,514
I'm going to keep you on the defensive.

292
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:28,560
Attack now, with any monster, and you
will instantly activate this trap card.

293
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:30,557
That Weevil's got Yugi cornered.

294
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,517
Yeah, he can't even counterattack.

295
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:37,317
As long as my trap card remains in play,
you're powerless to make a move against me.

296
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:41,060
So, does my tightening
wear make you squirm?

297
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:44,997
He's so busy bragging, he's not
paying any attention to my moves.

298
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:48,640
Maybe I can set a little trap
of my own. Face it, Yugi.

299
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:50,237
I've got you pinned down.

300
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:54,617
And while you're totally unable to attack
me, I can attack you any time I want.

301
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:57,540
Each turn you cower, I
create a new monster.

302
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:02,980
Keep drawing, Yugi.

303
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:05,477
My army of insects just
keeps getting bigger.

304
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:08,877
I'm going to wipe out all your
monsters in one bug blitzkrieg.

305
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,260
That's right, Weevil.

306
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,457
Put all your monsters on the field.

307
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:14,658
That's exactly what I'm counting on.

308
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:16,894
Just look at our Yugi.

309
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:19,120
He's so confident up there. I know.

310
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:22,917
When he's dueling, it's like he
becomes a totally different guy.

311
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,400
Well, what do you know?

312
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,740
I'm down to my last monstrous insect.

313
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,257
And you know what that means, Yugi.

314
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:30,117
You're about to be exterminated.

315
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:32,965
We'll see what my cards
have to say about that.

316
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:35,780
Yes, the Dark Magician. This is perfect.

317
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:39,022
There's no way Weevil can
resist him as a target.

318
00:18:39,180 --> 00:18:40,420
All right, Weevil.

319
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:43,140
I defend with a Dark Magician. Excellent.

320
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,637
I'll destroy your very
favorite card first.

321
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:48,160
Now, my pet, power up your laser cannon.

322
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,070
Attack!

323
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:57,680
Why are you laughing?

324
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,820
Weevil, you're not the only one
who can set a trap card. What?

325
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:06,397
You were so busy grandstanding, you paid
no attention to the cards I put into play.

326
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:09,740
But I thought they were all
monster-c-cards! Not all.

327
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:14,437
While you loaded the field with your bug
monsters, I prepared a special surprise.

328
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,900
The power of my Mirror Force Trap Card!

329
00:19:17,020 --> 00:19:18,160
Hold your fire!

330
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:19,740
Too late, Weevil.

331
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:22,637
You already ordered your
attack on my Dark Magician,

332
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:25,720
and Mirror Force will
deflect it right back at you!

333
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:29,800
My life points are devastated!

334
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:31,770
Yes!

335
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,317
Way to go!

336
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,230
Yeah, Yugi!

337
00:19:34,313 --> 00:19:37,580
He obliterated my army of beautiful bugs.

338
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,080
How dare he?

339
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:41,400
You're a liar and a cheat, Weevil.

340
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:44,877
But it was your overconfidence that
allowed me to get the best of you.

341
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,497
Your insects are decimated.

342
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:47,917
Your life points are low.

343
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:52,680
And as you yourself said before,
you have used up all your monsters.

344
00:19:54,740 --> 00:19:57,560
Actually, I lied about that, too. Huh?

345
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:01,837
I still have my most formidable
creature waiting in the wings.

346
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:06,120
And this unconquerable insect will
swat you down once and for all!
